abmod (1.0.19) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Fix the retry added in 1.0.18. It only noticed a device openwebrx had
    marked failed, and a device that dies on the way up is left marked nothing
    at all, so the retry never looked at it again and the receiver stayed down
    in silence. It now asks whether a device that should be running is
    running, reaps a dead process before starting a new one, and judges the
    result by whether the device is actually up.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:20:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.18) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Retry an SDR that failed to start, once a minute. openwebrx marks such a
    device failed and never tries it again for the life of the process, so a
    receiver whose radio is on another machine stayed dead after that machine
    rebooted. sdr_retry_interval sets the period; 0 switches it off.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.17) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Show everything the radio ID lookup already knows about a DMR caller:
    surname, town, state and country, not just the first name. The data was
    arriving and being discarded.
  * Name DMR talkgroups, so a call reads "222 (Italia)" rather than a bare
    number. The names come from BrandMeister's published list, one download of
    about 45 kB a week, cached on disk, never in the path a metadata frame
    takes. Set digital_voice_dmr_talkgroup_lookup to false to fetch nothing.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:45:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.16) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Stop looking for a sub-audible tone on modes that cannot carry one. CTCSS
    is an analogue FM arrangement; DMR, D-Star, YSF, NXDN and M17 have no room
    for it in the standard, and neither do AM or SSB. The detector now runs on
    narrowband FM only, and switching away clears the display instead of
    leaving a tone on screen.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:15:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.15) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Keep the gain asserted on a dongle served over the network. openwebrx
    sends it once, when it starts the connector, and never again when the
    connector merely reconnects - and rtl_tcp resets the tuner whenever a
    client connects. Any reconnection therefore left the receiver at minimum
    gain with every setting still reading correctly. The gain is now re-sent
    over the control socket every 30 seconds for rtl_tcp and soapy_remote
    devices.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.14) bullseye; urgency=low

  * The APRS parking now does nothing unless the igate itself is switched on.
    Feeding the igate is its only purpose, so with the igate off the clock is
    never started and the receiver stays on its saved frequency.
  * Say in the log why the parking did not happen: the igate is off, a
    listener is still connected, or a listener arrived while the clock ran.
    Those three used to be silent and read like a fault.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.13) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Fix the APRS parking never happening on a receiver whose saved default
    already is the APRS frequency: whether to park is now decided by where the
    radio is pointing, not by the default.
  * Fix the APRS parking coming back onto the parked frequency instead of the
    saved default: the saved centre frequency is now read from settings.json,
    because retuning writes the live configuration.
  * Arm the APRS idle clock at start-up as well, not only when a listener
    leaves. A receiver that had just been restarted and that nobody had
    visited since never parked, which is the one case the rule exists for.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.12) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Add the option to park the receiver on the APRS frequency while nobody is
    listening, and return to the saved centre frequency as soon as someone
    connects. Off by default.
  * Fix DMR producing nothing at all when a digital mode was switched on: the
    metadata chain now outputs FLOAT, so the secondary demodulator can still
    be wired to the audio buffer.
  * Put the remaining Italian comments and local names in the source into
    English.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.11) bullseye; urgency=low

  * Add a DMR mode that works without the AMBE codec: the chain stops at
    digiham's decoder, so radio IDs, talkgroups and timeslots are still
    reported, with no audio. Upstream's full chain is still used whenever a
    codec is present.
  * Document the CTCSS readout and the automatic direct sampling in the
    feature list, where they were missing.

 -- IU2QDA <iu2qda@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000

abmod (1.0.10) bullseye; urgency=low

